@using MultiShock.PluginSdk.Components
@page "/plugins/com-multishock-randomnodes/randomnodes"

<div class="space-y-4">
    <PageHeader Title="Random nodes" Icon="shuffle" Description="Add media status, randomness, text checks, time and delays to flows." />

    <div class="max-w-4xl space-y-4">
        <Card Title="Media nodes" Description="Read currently playing music from Windows media sessions, including local Spotify.">
            <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm">
                <li><span class="font-medium text-app-text">Spotify now playing</span>: song name, artist, album, length, current playtime, progress, and pause/play status.</li>
                <li><span class="font-medium text-app-text">Active media session</span>: the same metadata for whichever player Windows reports as active.</li>
            </ul>
        </Card>

        <Card Title="Utility nodes" Description="Small building blocks for adding randomness and quick logic to flows.">
            <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm">
                <li><span class="font-medium text-app-text">Random number</span>: generate a value between a min and max.</li>
                <li><span class="font-medium text-app-text">Random choice</span>: pick one comma- or line-separated choice.</li>
                <li><span class="font-medium text-app-text">Chance gate</span>: route flow by percentage chance.</li>
                <li><span class="font-medium text-app-text">Text contains</span>: branch based on a case-insensitive text match.</li>
                <li><span class="font-medium text-app-text">Time now</span>: output the current time string, local time, UTC time, Unix seconds, and day of week.</li>
                <li><span class="font-medium text-app-text">Format time</span>: convert seconds to mm:ss or a Unix timestamp to hh:mm AM/PM using local, UTC, or a manual offset.</li>
                <li><span class="font-medium text-app-text">Random delay</span>: wait a random duration before continuing.</li>
            </ul>
        </Card>

        <Alert Variant="info" Title="Spotify media session">
            The Spotify node uses the Windows media controls API, so Spotify must be running and exposing a media session.
            If Spotify is not found, the node falls back to the current Windows media session when available.
        </Alert>
    </div>
</div>
